  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Proposal**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the provided prompt and visual aids. \"MONTER\303\215A EN 3D\" is the title, with \"EXPLORACI\303\223N DIGITAL DE PREC\" as the subtitle, though I have not yet read the full title, or seen the entire image. My focus is on understanding the core concept and features suggested by the materials.\n\n\n**Defining the User Experience**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the user experience based on the provided button and navigation bar details. The \"EMPEZAR RECORRIDO\" button will take the user on a 3D tour, while the bottom navigation offers exploration, gallery, map, and settings. Each area gives interactivity. I\'m imagining the \"Explorer\" view as the central 3D hub, linking to a gallery, map, and settings. I see the map offering custom routes.\n\n\n**Refining the Interface**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the details for making this a high-quality web app, using a light theme. I plan to use the background toggle for a smooth transition across views, like floating HUD overlays, just like the original prototype. My focus is on the interactive 3D canvas viewer, with controls, landmarks, and audio. The explorer view will be the starting point.\n\n\n**Expanding the Core Features**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the core features. The landmark inspector will need audio ambiance and 3D hotspots. The gallery will require image links and modal views, categorized by architecture, nature, and history, along with notes. The map demands interactive pins, route filters, a search, and location cards. Finally, the settings will enable customization like background toggles, 3D rendering modes, sound controls, language switching, and itinerary export. I\'m also planning to incorporate three.js in the back end.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 917858011
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
