  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the initial structuring of the application now. I\'m focusing on defining the crucial data types in `src/types.ts`, which includes all the essential components like landmarks, map pins, gallery items, settings, view state, navigation tabs, audio, and 3D camera coordinates. I\'m also starting to flesh out the data with a detailed list of landmarks within `src/data/monteriaData.ts`.\n\n\n**Expanding Data and Components**\n\nI\'ve significantly expanded the data within `src/data/monteriaData.ts`, including high-resolution image URLs and pre-defined routes. I\'m also building out crucial UI components like `src/components/Header.tsx` for desktop and mobile, and a prototype bottom navigation bar in `src/components/BottomNav.tsx`. Now, I\'m focusing on the core interactive 3D viewport in `src/components/ThreeCanvas.tsx`, complete with river corridor terrain and architectural models.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Controls**\n\nI\'m now integrating floating markers for landmarks, which will feature click-to-inspect popups. Crucially, I\'m defining the 3D view controls: Orbit, Zoom, Reset Camera, Wireframe toggle, Day/Night toggle, and Flight/Orbit modes. I\'m also planning live telemetry overlays for altitude, coordinates, and orientation, alongside a compass widget to improve navigation. The primary Explorer view will be centered and have a title, button, and telemetry overlays. Clicking the button will activate the full HUD with interactive cards and audio.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 877316005
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
