  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Low-Poly Monteria**\n\nI\'m currently focused on redesigning the 3D scene in `ThreeCanvas.tsx` to create a low-poly representation of Monter\303\255a. I\'m starting by thinking about the urban layout and grid to ensure authenticity. The goal is to build a low-poly city generator to create this compelling scene.\n\n\n**Defining City Blocks**\n\nI\'ve been mapping the urban layout. The R\303\255o Sin\303\272\'s meandering path is now set, flowing smoothly. The riverside boulevard is taking shape with palm trees and docks. The Metal Bridge\'s green/teal truss is being visualized. A structured grid of streets is forming rectangular city blocks and the two banks are considered. The plaza with cathedral is also starting to come to life.\n\n\n**Refining Color Palette**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color palette. I\'m exploring stucco and colonial wall shades. Warm sand and Caribbean pastels are also being considered. I\'m choosing wood finish tones for doors, balconies, and window frames, as well as a modern commercial facade with tinted glass.\n\n\n**Visualizing Key Landmarks**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific landmarks to refine the city\'s identity. Catedral San Jer\303\263nimo\'s colonial architecture, the steel truss of Puente Met\303\241lico Rojas Pinilla, and the wooden docks of Muelle Tur\303\255stico & Planchones are being brought into the low-poly design. I\'m also visualizing the spiral Monumento al Porro on a roundabout plaza and the lush green Ronda del Sin\303\272 park.\n\n\n"
