  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Monter\303\255a\'s Generator**\n\nI\'m starting the design for a low-poly generator, targeting ThreeCanvas.tsx. Initial focus is on materials, specifically a Monter\303\255a-inspired palette. I\'ve begun defining wall materials, including `#fbf9f4`, `#f3eee3`, `#ebdfcb`, `#ded3ba`, and `#e0aa62` for building walls. I intend to use these colors in the design.\n\n\n**Defining Material Parameters**\n\nI\'ve expanded the material definition significantly, creating specific palettes for walls, roofs, vegetation, infrastructure, and the river. Wall colors now include colonial ochre, coastal teal, terracotta, and a soft bluish-grey. Roof materials range from vibrant to dark terracotta shades, and I\'ve established vegetation and nature color variations, including specific shades for Guayacan blossoms. Infrastructure materials now include street asphalt, sidewalk, bridge metal, river water, and wood.\n\n\n**Outlining Building Archetypes**\n\nI\'m now outlining key building archetypes to guide the low-poly generation. I\'m focusing on three main types: Colonial Houses with gabled roofs, Townhouses with rooftop terraces, and Mid-Rise Urban Buildings. Each type will have distinct characteristics: size, shape, color palettes, and specific accent features. I am also working on a process for creating unique landmarks.\n\n\n**Constructing Key Landmarks**\n\nI\'m now detailing Monter\303\255a\'s prominent landmarks. I\'ve designed the Front portal entrance, complete with three arched doorways, and its adjacent Square (Parque Sim\303\263n Bol\303\255var) featuring palm trees, benches, and a central monument. Next is the Puente Met\303\241lico Gustavo Rojas Pinilla, which includes the road deck and steel truss structure and pier supports. Finally, the Muelle Tur\303\255stico is underway, incorporating a wooden boardwalk with traditional Planchones del Sin\303\272.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 20
      nanos: 432299837
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
