    thinking: "**Defining Visual Identity**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the visual identity. Specifically, I\'m exploring a claymorphism/toy-town aesthetic for the architecture and environment of Monter\303\255a. My initial emphasis is on the facade palette, leaning toward soft cream and off-white clay tones to establish a distinct look.\n\n\n**Expanding Color Palette Details**\n\nI\'ve been expanding the color palette, focusing on specific hues for architectural elements. I\'m considering options like pale peach, pastel coral pink, and minty sage pastel for facades. Roofs will feature terracotta coral, coral peach, and warm clay red. I\'m also exploring window and door designs, like multi-pane windows and wooden clay doors with awnings. The street grid is slated for a light/medium grey asphalt plane.\n\n\n**Refining Environment Details**\n\nI\'m now refining environmental details. I\'m focusing on the street and flora for Monter\303\255a, aiming for a consistent aesthetic. Lane markings will be crisp white, while sidewalks will have beveled pastel curbs. For flora, I\'m envisioning fluffy cloud-like trees in bright lime or yellow, with chocolate-toned trunks, and pastel mint bushes. The Sin\303\272 River will be a clean pastel cyan ribbon with geometric flow lines and clay banks.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
