    thinking: "**Analyzing Navigation Issues**\n\nOkay, I\'m now digging into the unresponsive navigation bar buttons (Explorer, Gallery, Map, Settings). Focusing on the \"Interaction Layer,\" and trying to pin down the root cause of the click failures. I suspect there may be issues with event handling or propagation that is blocking the clicks, so I\'m investigating how those buttons are interacting with the touch event, and how they call the appropriate interactions.\n\n\n**Investigating Z-Index Conflicts**\n\nI\'ve determined that the lower navigation bar needs a high `z-index` and `pointer-events: auto` in the CSS to ensure it sits on top of the 3D canvas and registers clicks properly. Additionally, each button\'s `onClick` event in React must be examined to verify that they accurately trigger the view changes and selected button highlighting. I need to ensure event propagation isn\'t blocked by the 3D scene. I\'m focusing on `App.tsx` and how `isTourActive` impacts `activeTab` changes. There might be some issues switching tabs to or from \'explorer\' in tour mode.\n\n\n**Refining Bottom Navigation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the `BottomNav` component and making refinements. I\'ve confirmed `z-index: 50` and `pointer-events: auto` for the `<nav>` element. I\'m adding unique IDs to buttons and explicitly setting `type=\"button\"` with `onClick` to ensure reliable event handling. The event propagation is getting controlled through `e.stopPropagation()` and `onTabChange` calls. I\'m also going to clarify the active state highlighting!\n\n\n**Verifying Layering and Events**\n\nI\'m now checking layering and event handling in `App.tsx` and `BottomNav.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m ensuring `ThreeCanvas` container in `App.tsx` has `z-30 pointer-events-auto`, while bottom navigation has `z-50 pointer-events-auto`. Also, confirming `main` in `App.tsx` has padding so content isn\'t obscured by the `BottomNav`, and that all views can receive pointer events, to ensure correct behaviour.\n\n\n**Confirming Click Propagation**\n\nNow, I\'m analyzing the `BottomNav` component in detail, specifically the Explorer and Gallery buttons. I am making sure `e.stopPropagation()` is correctly preventing click events from bubbling up and interfering with other layers. Furthermore, I\'ve confirmed that each button is a `type=\"button\"` with an assigned `onClick` event and appropriate classNames. I am making sure the state and styling work.\n\n\n**Validating Tab Transitions**\n\nI\'m now closely reviewing the `BottomNav` component\'s structure. I\'ve re-examined the Gallery, Map, and Settings buttons, particularly their event handling and styling. I confirmed they have `type=\"button\"`, and use `e.stopPropagation()` and `onTabChange` calls for robust transition behavior. I am also checking state management for the active tab state and how it translates into UI changes.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Modal Visibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on `LandmarkModal.tsx` and verifying its `z-index`. I\'m updating it to `z-[70]` to ensure it always renders on top of other content, specifically the `BottomNav`. I\'m also confirming proper event handling and that the modal\'s interactivity is not blocked by lower layers.\n\n\n"
