    thinking: "**Analyzing Pointer Events**\n\nI\'ve started exploring pointer events, specifically focusing on tracking drag distances. I\'ve set up a system to record the initial pointer position on \"pointerdown.\" This will be essential for calculating movement and responsiveness in the drag interaction. The next step involves capturing movement events and calculating distances.\n\n\n**Refining Event Handling**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the click detection logic using `pointerUp`. If the pointer travel distance is small, I treat the event as a click, triggering raycasting. Otherwise, it is a drag. I\'m also examining the `controlsRef` and camera transitions. I\'ve defined the refs needed: `controlsRef`, `isAnimatingRef`, `targetLookAtRef`, `targetCamPosRef` and `ISO_OFFSET`. I\'m checking the initial camera setup and initial landmark selection upon mount for smooth camera transitions.\n\n\n**Implementing Camera Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on camera behavior and how it interacts with landmarks. I\'ve defined how the camera should look at and position itself relative to an initial landmark, storing the target positions. I\'m also implementing the `OrbitControls` configuration, disabling rotation to maintain the isometric view. Zoom and pan are enabled. I\'ve set up event listeners for control interactions, notably to stop animations when panning starts.\n\n\n"
