  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining ThreeCanvas Logic**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `ThreeCanvas.tsx` component. I\'ve introduced `controlsRef`, `isAnimatingRef`, and `targetLookAtRef` using `useRef`. These should help manage the camera controls, animation state, and the look-at target more effectively within the component\'s lifecycle. These additions set the stage for more complex interactions later on.\n\n\n**Implementing Camera Controls**\n\nI\'ve just added camera control configuration to my component. I\'ve disabled rotation in `OrbitControls`, while enabling panning and zooming, including screen-space panning. I\'ve also set mouse and touch interactions accordingly. I\'ve also implemented an event listener, so when the user starts interacting, `isAnimatingRef` will be set to false. Finally, I\'ve implemented a starting position/focus, and added an event listener to respond to `selectedLandmark` updates.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 9628354
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
